---
const steps = [
  {
    number: '01',
    title: 'Systems audit',
    body: 'We map where work enters, where it stalls, and which tool owns the truth. You leave with a written system diagram and a scoped build plan — whether or not we build together.',
    hue: 'var(--node-amber)',
  },
  {
    number: '02',
    title: 'Design the graph',
    body: 'I sketch the workflow architecture: triggers, data contracts, sub-workflows, fallbacks, and the order things fail in. Nothing is built until the plan is approved.',
    hue: 'var(--node-teal)',
  },
  {
    number: '03',
    title: 'Build & hand over',
    body: 'Workflows are built and tested against real payloads, documented, and deployed with monitoring in place. You keep ownership of every account and credential.',
    hue: 'var(--node-violet)',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="process">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>From audit to deployed in three steps</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        No discovery theatre. Each step ends with something you can read, review, or run.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="process">
      {steps.map((step) => (
        <li class="step" style={`--hue:${step.hue}`}>
          <span class="step-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="step-body">
            <span class="step-number">{step.number}</span>
            <h3>{step.title}</h3>
            <p>{step.body}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <p class="process-note">
      Scope and price are agreed before the build starts. If the audit shows automation is not
      worth it, I will say so.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .process {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .step {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0 0 2rem 1.9rem;
  }

  .step::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 5px;
    top: 1rem;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
  }

  .step:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .step:last-child::before {
    display: none;
  }

  .step-node {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.28rem;
    width: 11px;
    height: 11px;
    border: 2px solid var(--hue);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .step-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    align-content: start;
  }

  .step-number {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .step-body h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .step-body p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .process {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .step {
      padding: 1.85rem 1.5rem 0 0;
    }

    .step:not(:first-child) {
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
      border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .step::before {
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      top: 0;
      bottom: auto;
      width: auto;
      height: 1px;
    }

    .step-node {
      top: -5px;
    }

    .step:not(:first-child) .step-node {
      left: 1.5rem;
    }
  }

  .process-note {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-top: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }
</style>
